Z||000010||FieroSTETZ||01-09-2001||11:12 AM||||not too limited, but i also went with a high performance clutch, not an oem replacement. i went by smokey's advice, he has been helping me out since i used to have my 1972 duster, providing all kinds of hi po goodies. oh, btw, i found a local 2 seater sports car club near me, mr2's, x1/9's, fieros, miatas, etc- gonna join, see if i can't get some of these people online! wish i coulda gotten to know the people earlier, then i woulda bugged someone for clutch help.<P>when installin ght eclutch without taking anything outta the car, was it hard to get it aligned properly? also, how hard is it to get the flywheel out that way, mine will definately need to be resurfaced, has been slipping for about 2 weeks||||reg||1
